<title>
Brake Stroke Sensor Inspection and Adjustment
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AB106008001">
<title>
Inspection
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove brake stroke sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0AB106007"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check brake stroke sensor output voltage as follows.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, replace brake stroke sensor.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Arrange 3 new 1.5 V batteries (1) in series, and check that total voltage is 4.5 to 5.0 V.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Connect voltmeter (2) and batteries to brake stroke sensor as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFN10P132004.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "44.159mm" ver = "01" gw = "145" gh = "109"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
While moving lever end (1) manually, check that voltage varies depending on lever position as shown in the following graph.
</ptxt>
<figure>
